        "original_id": "d10fa950-04d1-55e5-ad93-a9f998bc795a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pedro Calomino, Law Adam, Amedeo Biavati, Ronaldo Luís Nazário de Lima\n- Concepts: Step over, scissors move\n- Roles: Striker, professional footballer\n\nFacts:\n- Pedro Calomino reportedly invented the step over move in the early 1900s.\n- Law Adam reportedly first used the step over move in Europe in the late 1920s and early 1930s.\n- Law Adam was famous for the move and earned the nickname \"Adam the Scissorsman.\"\n- Amedeo Biavati also used the step over move in Italy in the 1930s.\n- Ronaldo popularised the step over move in the mid-1990s.\n- Ronaldo Luís Nazário de Lima was born on 18 September 1976.\n- Ronaldo Luís Nazário de Lima is a Brazilian retired professional footballer who played as a striker.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "76e9ad6a-e0a4-5ee7-bffe-725f99aa029d",
        "text": "Page: Step over. Sentence: The move was reportedly invented by Argentine striker Pedro Calomino in the early 1900s.\nPage: Step over. Sentence: It was reportedly first used in Europe by Dutch player Law Adam, who was famous for it in the late 1920s/early 1930s, earning the nickname \"Adam the Scissorsman\", and it was later also used in Italy by Amedeo Biavati in the 1930s.\nPage: Step over. Sentence: It was popularised in the mid-1990s by global superstar Ronaldo.\nPage: Ronaldo (Brazilian footballer). Sentence: Ronaldo Luís Nazário de Lima (] ; born 18 September 1976), commonly known as Ronaldo, is a Brazilian retired professional footballer who played as a striker.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
